    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">affectŭōsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adf-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		adfectus, in later Lat., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of inclination</i>, <i>affection</i>, or <i>love; affectionate</i>, <i>kind</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piam adfectuosamque rem fecisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 11</span></i>
			; so 
			
			<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Ep. 5, 2</span></i>; Tert. c. Marc. 5,
			14.— <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adfectŭōsē</span></b> , <i>affectionately</i>, etc.,
				<i><span class="en">Cassiod. Ep. 3, 4</span></i>.—<i>Sup.</i>, <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4,
			11</span></i>.</div>
